b. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive health services by trained health personnel at Community Health Centers and at Hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level up to court decisions on cases of Violence against Women and Children;
f. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women and Child Victims of Violence; and
h. coverage of social reintegration services for Women and Child Victims of Violence.

Article 6
Sexual violence as referred to in Article 3 letter c is caused by:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner;
and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with another person for commercial purposes and or specific purposes.

